Add esp32c3 (RISC-V rv32imc) as a BUILD-ONLY firmware target to the @embedded
(firmware) module: a new board platform + cc_toolchain, the c3 branch of the
board/pins/arduino-core selects, and a parallel esp32c3 section of the
generated @arduino_esp32 scaffold (mirrors the C6 recipe with the arch dropped
to rv32imc — no atomics — and the ESP32C3_DEV board defines).

Scope is build-gating only: the image is NOT expected to be runtime-correct on
real c3 silicon yet (e.g. firmware/netstack's ccmp.rs hardcodes the C6 AES/PCR
register map). The c3 SDK is staged by the companion
embedded-esp32-libs-c6-c3.patch (extends the FOD to unzip esp32c3/ too).

Edits:
 - rules/firmware.bzl: esp32c3 -> //platforms:esp32c3 in _BOARD_PLATFORM +
   the `board` attr allowlist (the esptool chip name IS "esp32c3").
 - platforms/BUILD.bazel: esp32c3_board constraint_value, esp32c3 platform
   (riscv32 + os:none + esp32c3_board), is_esp32c3 config_setting.
 - toolchains/cc/esp32c3/BUILD.bazel (new): cc_toolchain gated to
   //platforms:esp32c3_board, base arch -march=rv32imc_zicsr_zifencei
   -mabi=ilp32 (mirrors esp32c6).
 - MODULE.bazel: register //toolchains/cc/esp32c3:cc_toolchain; add the
   riscv32imc-unknown-none-elf Rust triple.
 - libs/board/BUILD.bazel: is_esp32c3 branches (core_esp32c3, esp32c3.cpp) +
   esp32c3_bootloader_bin genrule.
 - libs/board/esp32c3.cpp (new): board LED support (mirrors esp32c6.cpp).
 - libs/pins/BUILD.bazel: is_esp32c3 LED_DATA_PIN (GPIO8, C3-DevKitC-1).
 - nix/arduino_esp32.BUILD: parallel esp32c3 chip-specific targets
   (sdk_*_esp32c3, core_esp32c3 with from-source mbedtls + ssl wraps) AND
   esp32c3 variants of the bundled Arduino libraries (network/fs/wifi/hash/ble/
   preferences/webserver_esp32c3) built against sdk_hdrs_esp32c3 — so a c3 image
   carries ONE (c3) IDF include set, not c6+c3 (which overflowed g++ -> cc1plus argv).
 - libs/vendor/BUILD.bazel: the wifi/webserver/ble/preferences aliases select
   the per-chip variant (is_esp32c3 -> *_esp32c3).

